      <div class="article__main">
        <div class="article__body prose">
          <blockquote>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Do 6 things: finish the pre-load, keep <strong>more than 212 GB</strong> free, update your console, check your account, charge your controller, and look at your countdown.</li>
<li><strong>Unlock time:</strong> midnight in your time zone on <strong>Thu 19 Nov 2026</strong> (00:00 CET in Slovenia). New Zealand unlocked first, at 12:00 CET on Wed 18 Nov.</li>
<li><strong>GTA 6 targets 30 FPS</strong> (30 pictures per second) on PS5, PS5 Pro and Xbox Series X|S. No 60 FPS mode is announced, so do not search for one.</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Words used on this page.</strong> <em>Pre-load</em> means downloading the game early. <em>Account</em> is your PlayStation or Xbox profile. <em>Rest Mode</em> (PS5) or <em>Sleep mode</em> (Xbox) means the console is on at low power.</p>
<h2 id="step-1-check-the-pre-load-is-finished" tabindex="-1">Step 1: Check the pre-load is finished</h2>
<p><strong>PS5</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>PS button</strong> to open the Control Center.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Downloads/Uploads</strong>.</li>
<li>Find <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong>. It must not be paused or waiting.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Xbox Series X|S</strong> <em>(general Xbox menu path, check on your console)</em></p>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>Xbox button</strong>.</li>
<li>Open <strong>My games &amp; apps</strong>, then <strong>Queue</strong>.</li>
<li>Check GTA VI is not in the queue. If it is there, it is still downloading or paused.</li>
</ol>
<p>![PS5 Downloads/Uploads screen with GTA VI finished](TODO: image:launch-night-checklist-step-1 — menu screen, PS5: Control Center &gt; Downloads/Uploads showing the GTA VI download completed)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. PS5 Downloads/Uploads with GTA VI finished.</em></p>
<p>Stuck? See <a href="preload-size.md">the download fix steps</a>.</p>
<h2 id="step-2-check-free-space" tabindex="-1">Step 2: Check free space</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>PS5:</strong> open <strong>Settings &gt; Storage</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Xbox:</strong> press the <strong>Xbox button</strong>, open <strong>Profile &amp; system &gt; Settings &gt; System &gt; Storage devices</strong>.</li>
<li>You need <strong>more than 212 GB free</strong> for the game, plus a gap for updates.</li>
</ol>
<p>![storage screen with free space](TODO: image:launch-night-checklist-step-2 — menu screen, PS5 and Xbox storage screens side by side with free space circled)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. Where to read your free space on PS5 and Xbox.</em></p>
<h2 id="step-3-turn-on-automatic-updates" tabindex="-1">Step 3: Turn on automatic updates</h2>
<p><strong>PS5</strong> (official PlayStation steps)</p>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Settings &gt; Saved Data and Game/App Settings &gt; Automatic Updates</strong>.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Auto-Install in Rest Mode</strong>.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Settings &gt; System &gt; Power Saving &gt; Features Available in Rest Mode</strong>.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Stay Connected to the Internet</strong>.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Settings &gt; System &gt; System Software &gt; System Software Update and Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Download Update Files Automatically</strong> and <strong>Install Update Files Automatically</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Xbox Series X|S</strong> <em>(general Xbox menu path, check on your console)</em></p>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>Xbox button</strong>, then open <strong>Profile &amp; system &gt; Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Open <strong>System &gt; Updates</strong>.</li>
<li>Turn on the options to keep your console and your games up to date.</li>
</ol>
<p>![PS5 automatic updates settings](TODO: image:launch-night-checklist-step-3 — menu screen, PS5: Automatic Updates with Auto-Install in Rest Mode switched on)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. PS5 Automatic Updates with Auto-Install in Rest Mode on.</em></p>
<h2 id="step-4-check-your-account" tabindex="-1">Step 4: Check your account</h2>
<ol>
<li>Check you are signed in to the account that <strong>bought the game or entered the code</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>PS5, shared console:</strong> open <strong>Settings &gt; Users and Accounts &gt; Other &gt; Console Sharing and Offline Play</strong> and select <strong>Enable</strong>. Then other accounts can play too.</li>
<li>Check your order. <strong>PS5:</strong> sign in, select your avatar, select <strong>Order History</strong>, and check the GTA VI order says successful.</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="step-5-controller-and-picture" tabindex="-1">Step 5: Controller and picture</h2>
<ol>
<li>Charge your controller to full. Keep a charging cable close.</li>
<li><strong>PS5 only:</strong> run HDR setup at <strong>Settings &gt; Screen and Video &gt; Video Output &gt; Adjust HDR</strong>. This is general PS5 advice, not a GTA 6 setting.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Game Mode</strong> in your TV menu. The name varies by TV.</li>
<li><strong>DualSense haptics (buzz) and adaptive triggers (stiff buttons)</strong> are supported on PS5. You can change them in the game’s accessibility settings. The exact menu name is not announced yet.</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="step-6-at-the-unlock-moment" tabindex="-1">Step 6: At the unlock moment</h2>
<ol>
<li>Start GTA VI a few minutes early. It will still be locked.</li>
<li>At your unlock time, start it again.</li>
<li>If the game offers an update, install it. Its size is not announced.</li>
<li>Servers may be busy. If it will not start, wait 5 minutes and try again before you delete anything.</li>
<li>Do <strong>not</strong> change your region or use a second account to unlock early. Rockstar, Sony and Microsoft have not endorsed it, and it is unconfirmed that it works.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Xbox One owners:</strong> you stream through Xbox Cloud Gaming from <strong>1 AM ET on 19 Nov</strong>, at Xbox Series S graphics settings. Starting 11 Nov, in supported markets, you can buy cloud playtime without Game Pass (Xbox Wire).</p>
<h2 id="quick-fixes" tabindex="-1">Quick fixes</h2>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Problem</th>
<th>Do this</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Download stuck</td>
<td><strong>PS5:</strong> open Downloads/Uploads, select GTA VI, <strong>Pause</strong>, then <strong>Resume</strong>. Still stuck: <strong>Cancel and Delete</strong>, then download again from <strong>Game Library</strong>. <strong>Xbox:</strong> open the <strong>Queue</strong>, highlight GTA VI, press the <strong>Menu button</strong>, pause, then resume.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Not enough space</td>
<td>Free more than 212 GB. Delete or move another game.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Wrong account</td>
<td>Sign out. Sign in to the account that bought the game.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Box code will not work</td>
<td>Check the code and your region. Ask the shop if the code is missing or unreadable. Ask PlayStation or Xbox Support for code problems.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Bug after launch</td>
<td>Contact Rockstar Support. We will post verified fixes after launch.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>![checklist graphic with six steps](TODO: image:launch-night-checklist-step-4 — diagram, our own art: a 6-step checklist poster with icons for download, storage, updates, account, controller, countdown)
<em>Caption: Diagram. The six launch night steps on one poster.</em></p>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="what-should-i-do-before-gta-6-unlocks" tabindex="-1">What should I do before GTA 6 unlocks?</h3>
<p>Finish the pre-load, free more than 212 GB, turn on updates, check your account, charge your controller and check your countdown.</p>
<h3 id="do-i-have-to-stay-up-for-midnight" tabindex="-1">Do I have to stay up for midnight?</h3>
<p>Only if you want to play at midnight. The game will be ready when you start it.</p>
<h3 id="is-there-a-performance-mode" tabindex="-1">Is there a performance mode?</h3>
<p>Not announced. Rockstar says 30 FPS on current consoles.</p>
<h3 id="will-servers-be-busy" tabindex="-1">Will servers be busy?</h3>
<p>Sony and Microsoft both say pre-orders were record-breaking, so expect busy servers.</p>
